# Future Improvements

## Test Executor Pattern Enhancement

### Current State (Working)

Tests import definitions and map handlers:
```typescript
import { modelLoadLlm } from '../../test-definitions.ts';

class ModelExecutor {
  handlers = {
    [modelLoadLlm.testId]: this.loadLlm,
  };
  
  async loadLlm(params: typeof modelLoadLlm.params, expectation: typeof modelLoadLlm.expectation) {
    // Implementation
  }
}
```

**Pros**: Works, navigable, type-safe params
**Cons**: Still requires handlers map boilerplate, some casting in execute()

### Proposed Enhancement

Create helper that generates strongly-typed handlers from test definitions:

```typescript
abstract class BaseExecutor {
  // Shared state and logic
  llmModelId: string | null = null;
  
  protected validateModel(modelId: string | null, expectation) { ... }
  protected validateText(text: string, expectation) { ... }
}

const executors = [
  createTestHandler(modelLoadLlm, BaseExecutor, async function(params) {
    this.llmModelId = await loadModel({...});
    return this.validateModel(this.llmModelId);
  }),
  
  createTestHandler(completionStreaming, BaseExecutor, async function(params) {
    if (!this.llmModelId) { /* load */ }
    const result = await completion({...});
    return this.validateText(result, this.expectation);
  }),
];

// Single executor with all tests
export const executor = createExecutor({ handlers: executors });
```

**Benefits**:
- ✅ Fully type-safe params/expectation (no unknown, no casting)
- ✅ Inheritance for shared logic (base classes)
- ✅ No handlers map boilerplate
- ✅ State sharing across tests (llmModelId persists)
- ✅ Cleaner syntax

**Implementation needed**:
- createTestHandler<T extends TestDefinition> helper
- Base executor classes with common patterns
- Type extraction from test definitions

**Priority**: Post-MVP (current pattern works fine for 100+ tests)

